      "worked_solution": "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n{0}^{∘}\\le \\theta \\le {180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and second quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{2}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/ca39c4cde40b99fd40a11746a31398d82814268b2df706e3101ee88648c9e2d4.png)\n\nFrom the values in the second quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\ncos\\,({120}^{∘})=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\narccos\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})={120}^{∘}.\n$$",
